    {
        "user": "UP00ZLX6G",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1729592929.315379",
        "client_msg_id": "d8c4e0ad-6850-4a4a-b4ac-cf56e5bd7d5e",
        "text": "Neat explorations! :heart: the name :smile:\n\nWas digging into the <https://github.com/inkandswitch/inkling/tree/main|code> and wondering why you have an iOS wrapper? Are there limitations with web gestures in the provided browser?\n\nOne of my side projects ages ago was to do with doing gestures on a webpage, so I\u2019m interested in the stack :pancakes:",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1729549918.845699",
        "parent_user_id": "UC2A2ARPT",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "s/cSy",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "Neat explorations! "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "emoji",
                                "name": "heart",
                                "unicode": "2764-fe0f"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " the name "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "emoji",
                                "name": "smile",
                                "unicode": "1f604"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "\n\nWas digging into the "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "link",
                                "url": "https://github.com/inkandswitch/inkling/tree/main",
                                "text": "code"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " and wondering why you have an iOS wrapper? Are there limitations with web gestures in the provided browser?\n\nOne of my side projects ages ago was to do with doing gestures on a webpage, so I\u2019m interested in the stack "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "emoji",
                                "name": "pancakes",
                                "unicode": "1f95e"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ]
    },
    {
        "user": "UC2A2ARPT",
        "type": "message",
        "ts": "1729606884.776249",
        "client_msg_id": "b456d1d0-2069-4291-95fe-f08b077408ca",
        "text": "<@UBN9AFS0N> Fantastic. An explicit goal was to make something with CSS that looks as different as possible in each (current/recent) browser. So far you're winning \"most cursed\"\n\n<@UP00ZLX6G> Yes, there is one nasty limitation in WebKit \u2014 it only gives you events for the fingers _or_ the pen, not both at once, and it doesn't give you much info from each of them. So our Swift wrapper forwards full-fidelity, low latency pencil (at 240hz) and touch (at 120hz), with all the fanciness (tilt angle, barrel roll, pressure, etc) across to the JS context. We've been using this technique since back in Crosscut/Inkling, and I recently rewrote the project to be much simpler (a single Swift file). Hoping to pull it out into its own repo and share it with a little write up. We'll see. Either way, it's great for iPad prototyping, and I encourage everyone to play around with it!",
        "team": "T5TCAFTA9",
        "thread_ts": "1729549918.845699",
        "parent_user_id": "UC2A2ARPT",
        "blocks": [
            {
                "type": "rich_text",
                "block_id": "6klt0",
                "elements": [
                    {
                        "type": "rich_text_section",
                        "elements": [
                            {
                                "type": "user",
                                "user_id": "UBN9AFS0N"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " Fantastic. An explicit goal was to make something with CSS that looks as different as possible in each (current/recent) browser. So far you're winning \"most cursed\"\n\n"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "user",
                                "user_id": "UP00ZLX6G"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": " Yes, there is one nasty limitation in WebKit \u2014 it only gives you events for the fingers "
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "or ",
                                "style": {
                                    "italic": true
                                }
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "text",
                                "text": "the pen, not both at once, and it doesn't give you much info from each of them. So our Swift wrapper forwards full-fidelity, low latency pencil (at 240hz) and touch (at 120hz), with all the fanciness (tilt angle, barrel roll, pressure, etc) across to the JS context. We've been using this technique since back in Crosscut/Inkling, and I recently rewrote the project to be much simpler (a single Swift file). Hoping to pull it out into its own repo and share it with a little write up. We'll see. Either way, it's great for iPad prototyping, and I encourage everyone to play around with it!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "reactions": [
            {
                "name": "heart",
                "users": [
                    "U04Q53X6P7W",
                    "UP00ZLX6G"
                ],
                "count": 2
            }
        ]
    },
